Workshop is a large and luminous room. There are lots of incomprehensible devices and tools. Nikolas, dressed in black overall is standing by the workbench, grinding some part with a file. By the workbench you can see something between dummy and knightly armour. There are gears in figure's chest.
"Father calls him a golem", quietly says Doyle. "He's joking, of course, golems exist only in tales. This is a robot."
"A robot?" you ask, "can he think?".
"No, not yet. It's hard to make a machine that can think by itself. Father will operate it from the control panel".
"And what is that?" you ask pointing at a flat metal box with round metal wheel on one side.
"We called it a lighter," says Doyle, "there is benzine inside. When you turn the wheel, sparks are produced, and benzine catches fire. More convenient than matches".
"Shall we take it with us, just in case?"
"Ok".
Doyle puts the lighter in his pocket. At the same time Nikolas noticed you.
"Hello, boys!" he smiles. "Would you like me to tell you about my golem?".
You secretly pull Doyle's sleeve, but it's too late. You don't want to offend Nikolas, so you patiently listen to him. Time flies and you constantly look at the clock. And finally, when the moment is right, you make an excuse, and say that you have to go.  